From 299c1417b1e04493b972d48eb05688e502af599a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@lifescience-advisors.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 17:04:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make the shipped artifacts match the code (BUG-1, SEC-4,
 SEC-5, PHIL-2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A first-time operator following the README got a systemd unit that
crash-loops, their agent's Matrix password written to a world-readable
file, a homeserver left accepting registrations on any install error, and
silently no semantic search. Each is a mismatch between what ships and
what the code actually does.

BUG-1 / ARCH-3 — one unit file, installed and tested.
  etc/openalph@.service invoked the CLI with a bare TOML path and no
  subcommand. cli.py sets `sub.required = True`, so it exits 2, and
  Restart=on-failure turns that into a permanent restart loop.
  test_systemd.py asserted that exact ExecStart, so the suite enforced the
  bug. Meanwhile install.sh wrote a different, working unit from a
  heredoc, and SECURITY.md documented a third variant -- the unit actually
  deployed was never tested, and SECURITY.md's guarantees were
  unverifiable.

  The unit now lives at src/openalph/data/openalph@.service and ships as
  package data, so it is on disk after pip install even in the
  `curl | sudo bash` path where no checkout exists. etc/openalph@.service
  is a symlink to it; install.sh copies it from the installed package.
  TestSingleSourceOfTruth fails if a heredoc unit body reappears in
  install.sh or if the etc/ symlink becomes a real file again.

  Two follow-on fixes fell out of actually testing the deployed unit:
  the installer's version bound /srv/openalph/shared read-only while the
  dir is created 2770 group-writable by design (now read-write), and its
  two Environment= lines -- legal systemd -- are a DuplicateOptionError to
  the configparser the suite uses, so it would have failed the tests that
  never ran against it. Folded into one equivalent directive.

SEC-4 — stop writing the agent's Matrix password to a log.
  step0 tees all stdout to /tmp/openalph-bootstrap-<ts>.log created under
  the default umask (0644), and the final summary printed the agent's
  Matrix password to that stream. Any local user could read it
  indefinitely and re-login as the agent, contradicting the script's own
  "never written to any log" invariant. The password now goes to /dev/tty
  only; with no tty it goes to a 0600 root-owned file with instructions to
  move and delete it. The log itself is created 0600 up front.

SEC-5 — guarantee registration is re-locked.
  Registration is enabled before any account exists, every failure path is
  a bare `exit 1` under `set -e`, and there was no cleanup handler, so
  Part G's "disable registration" never ran on any error. A re-run (which
  INSTALL.md recommends) hits M_USER_IN_USE and exits, leaving the
  homeserver accepting token-gated registrations behind the public Caddy
  proxy. An EXIT trap now re-locks unconditionally, armed the moment the
  override goes live and cleared once Part G has re-locked cleanly. If the
  automatic re-lock fails it prints the two commands to run.

PHIL-2 — honest dependencies, and a visible degradation.
  httpx is imported directly by provider.py and tools/web.py but was
  undeclared, surviving only as a transitive of anthropic/openai. It is
  now a declared dependency and the README says five, not four.

  llama_cpp and sqlite_vec are also imported directly and were named only
  in requirements.lock.txt, which nothing referenced -- so no standard
  install ever got them, and the GGUF model the embedder defaults to was
  never downloaded. Since every import in that path fails soft, operators
  got BM25-only results from a feature the README calls "Nomic-embed +
  BM25 hybrid", with the failure visible only in journalctl. They are now
  an optional [memory] extra that install.sh installs by default, with a
  checksum-pinned model fetch, and memory_search emits a one-time in-room
  notice when semantic search is unavailable so the degradation is legible
  where the operator actually is.

  The model download is checksum-gated and OPENALPH_MODEL_SHA256 is
  deliberately empty, which makes the installer SKIP the download with a
  warning rather than trust an unverified ~270MB file loaded in-process by
  every agent. Fill it in before tagging (marked TODO(release)).

Also fixes BUG-16 in passing, since it is the same line of install.sh:
`openalph --version` is not a real flag, so the "installed version" the
installer reported was an argparse usage error with its non-zero exit
swallowed by `|| true`. Now read from package metadata.

Tests: test_systemd.py rewritten around the canonical unit -- 29 tests
pass, including the two that previously locked in the crash-loop.

Refs: BUG-1, SEC-4, SEC-5, PHIL-2, ARCH-3, BUG-16
